WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.435
-We are so lucky to have

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.570
Fred Armisen back
with us tonight.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.272
Give it up for Fred right
over there.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.707
[ Cheering and applause ]
And, Fred, I'm always

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:09.709
so taken aback.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:10.810
You have so many projects.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.913
Not just film,
not just television,

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.081
not just music,

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.917
but just over a wide breadth
of interests.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:21.354
And I was just reading in the
trades, as you like to call it,

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:25.492
that you're launching your first
celebrity fragrance.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:26.693
-Yes.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.361
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:31.998
And, um, it's more like an --
it's like an ink than --

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.800
[ Laughter ]
So, it's like

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.236
this ink I'm putting out
that's like

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:39.672
it smells like -- it has like
a very pungent, inky smell.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.608
-Okay. Is it actually ink?
Like is it --

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:45.111
If you got it on yourself,
would it stain like ink?

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.046
-It's not about that.
It's about how it smells.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.948
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.
-So, it's got

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.517
a very sort of like
inky smell to it

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:54.320
and it's called TheFredArmisen.
-Okay.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.589
-And so you just --
-It's called TheFredArmisen?

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.291
-Yeah, as one word.
-Okay.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.658
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.658 --> 00:01:01.360
-Why did you choose
to make it one word?

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.028
-It was my organization.

00:01:03.028 --> 00:01:05.164
They choose it for me, so.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:06.632
[ Laughter ]
I have like a whole crew
of people

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:08.534
and they come up with all this
stuff and they are so --

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.136
-They don't even go to you
for approvals?

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.472
-No. They're so talented
and they're so smart.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.707
-Okay.
Do they bully you, Fred?

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.442
It seems like they might
bully you a little.

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:17.843
-In their own way,

00:01:17.843 --> 00:01:19.412
[ Laughter ]
which is fine. It doesn't --

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.412
you know, that's fine with me.

00:01:20.412 --> 00:01:22.915
But it's a nighttime fragrance.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:25.685
And, uh, so you just, you know,
like before you go out,

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:26.719
you just put it on.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:27.586
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:29.022
-But it doesn't stain like ink?

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.656
I want to make sure
because you're doing this

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:32.091
and I feel,
if it stains like ink,

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:33.259
I don't want to put it on.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.728
-It stains like ink,
but it doesn't matter.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.863
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:38.964
-It's really --
-It's the smell.

00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:40.133
-It's really exciting.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.000
Give it up for Fred Armisen,
everybody.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:42.936
[ Cheering and applause ]

